==English==

===Etymology===
{{uder|en|la|levō||I elevate, I lift up}}, from {{m|la|levis||light}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈlɛvɪteɪt/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-levitate.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cause to [[rise]] in the air and [[float]], as if in [[defiance]] of [[gravity]].
#: {{ux|en|The magician '''levitated''' the woman.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To be [[suspended]] in the air, as if in defiance of gravity.
#: {{ux|en|The guru claimed that he could '''levitate'''.}}

====Derived terms====
